# Sourcing is the only module that exposes minimal-API endpoints (not OData). RequestQuote is a
# command, not entity CRUD — it kicks off an async outbox-→-broker-→-supplier flow that ultimately
# fills in an IngredientQuote row. POST returns 202 Accepted with a Location header pointing to
# /api/sourcing/quotes/{id}; poll that to see the quote state transition (Pending → Received).
@host = 127.0.01:443
@baseUrl = https://{{host}}/api/sourcing/quotes

###
# @name RequestQuote
# SupplierKey must match an entry under
#   Modules:Sourcing:Procurement:IngredientSupply:Clients:Suppliers:<key>:Url
# in appsettings (Development includes "test-supplier" pointing at the local stub).
POST {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8
Cache-Control: no-cache

{
	"SupplierKey": "test-supplier",
	"RecipeId": 1,
	"Ingredients": [
		{ "Name": "spaghetti", "Quantity": 400, "Unit": "g" },
		{ "Name": "pancetta",  "Quantity": 150, "Unit": "g" }
	]
}

###
# @name GetQuoteById
GET {{baseUrl}}/1 HTTP/1.1
Host: {{host}}
Cache-Control: no-cache
